 "background": "Written and composed by Jonče Hristovski in 1964, in 14/8 time. A love song to Macedonian girls that became an unofficial anthem, especially in the diaspora. Danced as *pravo* or *lesno*. Hristovski (1931-2000) was born in Bitola and was a singer and composer of folk music who also performed with the Tanec national ensemble. His wife died in the 1963 Skopje earthquake after giving birth to their twin daughters; a year later he wrote his best-known song.",
